---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CountyMunicipalityMap from '../../../../components/jurisdictions/CountyMunicipalityMap.astro';
import PublicRecords from '../../../../components/jurisdictions/PublicRecords.astro';
import DeploymentStatusMeta from '../../../../components/jurisdictions/DeploymentStatusMeta.astro';
import { ogleMunicipalities, ogleMunicipalitySources } from '../../../../data/illinois/counties/ogle';
import { ogleCountyRecords } from '../../../../data/illinois/counties/ogle-records';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Ogle County Surveillance | NoRec.US"
  description="County and municipal surveillance research for Ogle County, Illinois, with jurisdiction boundaries, FOIA sources, and open research files."
  active="surveillance"
>
<main class="page_shell">
  <nav class="jurisdiction_breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/illinois/">Illinois</a><span>→</span><strong>Ogle County</strong>
  </nav>

  <header class="article_header">
    <p class="eyebrow">LOCAL SURVEILLANCE · OGLE COUNTY, ILLINOIS</p>
    <h1>Ogle County</h1>
    <p class="article_deck">This county batch establishes the municipal research structure and primary-record entry points. NoRec has not yet reviewed enough surveillance-specific primary records to publish a countywide technology inventory.</p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">MUNICIPALITIES · OFFICIAL BOUNDARIES</p>
    <h2>Drill down from Ogle County to the municipality.</h2>
    <p>The baseline comes from the Illinois State Archives local-government index, supplemented by Ogle County's own yearbook where the state index is incomplete for current incorporated geography. Rockford and Rochelle are marked as cross-county municipalities.</p>

    <div class="map_legend" aria-label="Municipality map legend">
      <span><i class="legend_swatch legend_covered"></i><strong>Research available</strong></span>
      <span><i class="legend_swatch legend_open"></i><strong>Unresearched</strong></span>
      <span><i class="legend_swatch legend_cross_county"></i><strong>Crosses county line</strong></span>
    </div>

    <CountyMunicipalityMap county="Ogle" municipalities={ogleMunicipalities} />

    <div class="jurisdiction_cards municipality_directory">
      {ogleMunicipalities.map(municipality => {
        const isRockford = municipality.slug === 'rockford';
        const href = isRockford
          ? '/illinois/counties/winnebago/cities/rockford/'
          : `/illinois/counties/ogle/cities/${municipality.slug}/`;
        return (
          <a href={href}>
            <strong>{municipality.name}</strong>
            <span>{municipality.form.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + municipality.form.slice(1)} · {municipality.status === 'documented' ? 'Municipal dossier available' : 'Research needed'}{municipality.crossCounty ? ` · crosses ${municipality.counties.join(' / ')} counties` : ''}</span>
          </a>
        );
      })}
    </div>

    <p class="map_note">
      <a href={ogleMunicipalitySources.stateArchives}>Illinois State Archives local-government index</a> ·
      <a href={ogleMunicipalitySources.countyYearbook}>Ogle County yearbook</a> ·
      <a href={ogleMunicipalitySources.censusCrossCounty}>U.S. Census cross-county geography notes</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="evidence_box evidence_unknown">
    <span class="status_label">RESEARCH NEEDED</span>
    <h2>County surveillance inventory not yet established.</h2>
    <p>NoRec has not yet reviewed enough primary records to publish a current Ogle County Sheriff inventory for ALPRs, fixed cameras, drones, social-media analytics, facial recognition, or related surveillance systems. Unknown means unverified, not absent.</p>
  </section>

  <PublicRecords records={ogleCountyRecords} />

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">NEXT RECORDS</p>
    <h2>High-value follow-up.</h2>
    <ul class="about_questions">
      <li>Current Ogle County Sheriff technology and equipment inventory.</li>
      <li>ALPR contracts, invoices, locations, retention settings, sharing configuration, and audit logs.</li>
      <li>Drone inventory, payloads, policy, and flight reports.</li>
      <li>County and municipal camera-system contracts and network diagrams.</li>
      <li>Social-media analytics, facial-recognition, and real-time crime-center software contracts or policies.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
